{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4463140","formula":"O₃F₂","hill":"F2O3","elements":["O","F"],"composition":{"F":2.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Difluorine trioxide","ru":"Триоксидифторид"},"descriptions":{"en":"Oxygen fluorides are compounds of elements oxygen and fluorine with the general formula OnF2, where n = 1 to 6. Many different oxygen fluorides are known: Oxygen monofluoride (OF) Oxygen difluoride (OF2) Dioxygen difluoride (O2F2) Trioxygen difluoride or ozone difluoride (O3F2) Tetraoxygen difluoride (O4F2) Pentaoxygen difluoride (O5F2) Hexaoxygen difluoride (O6F2) Dioxygen monofluoride or fluoroperoxyl (O2F) Oxygen fluorides are strong oxidizing agents with high energy and can release their energy either instantaneously or at a controlled rate. Thus, these compounds attracted much attention as potential oxidizers in jet propulsion systems."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":22061841,"mass":85.995,"charge":0,"smiles":"O(OF)OF","inchikey":"VVZRXWIVHSBDAU-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"fluoroperoxy hypofluorite","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"22061841","atoms":5,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.464,"y":-0.897,"z":0.071,"el":"F"},{"x":1.464,"y":-0.897,"z":0.071,"el":"F"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.909,"z":0.408,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.19,"y":0.443,"z":-0.275,"el":"O"},{"x":1.19,"y":0.443,"z":-0.275,"el":"O"}],"bonds":[[0,3,1],[1,4,1],[2,3,1],[2,4,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4463140","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trioxygen_difluoride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"properties","name":"PubChem","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/22061841","license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},{"role":"structure","name":"PubChem 3D","url":"https://pu